  <data name="GuideData" xml:space="preserve"><value>Sending and receiving</value></data>
  <data name="GuideDataBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Text uses the selected encoding. HEX accepts two-digit bytes with optional whitespace. Append CR, LF or CRLF with the line-ending option. Timed sending repeats at the chosen interval and stops on disconnect or error.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideReceive" xml:space="preserve"><value>Receive monitor and logs</value></data>
  <data name="GuideReceiveBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Pause affects the display only. The receive monitor keeps the latest 256K characters and can be cleared or exported. Serilog records each port's traffic and errors, rolling daily or at 10 MB and retaining 30 files.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideSave" xml:space="preserve"><value>Automatic saving</value></data>
  <data name="GuideSaveBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each port remembers its own configuration and payload. Layout, theme, language and selected port are saved automatically. Connections and timers must be started manually after restart.</value></data>
